@@ Calculate the "numerical derivative".
@@ ( function { x v } -- df/dx_approximation )
@@
@@ The { x v } parameter is a list of a single function parameter with its value.
@@ 
@@ See: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numerical_differentiation: five point midpoint approximation.
@@ The differentation approximation parameter h is not an absolute small value but h = x * d.
@@ Where d is a small value.
@@
@@ Note that we do not evaluate for x = v. v is not used at all.
@@ The calling command gets an expression back, that still needs to be evaluated.
@@ In that sense this derivative is not a completely numerical approximation.
@@ It is an algebraic approximation.
@@
@@ Example:
@@
@@ 'tgamma(x²)'
@@ { x 1 }
@@ NumericalDerivative
@@
@@ Expect: '((Gamma((X·1.00000 0001)²)-Gamma((X·0.99999 9999)²))·8+(Gamma((X·0.99999 9998)²)-Gamma((X·1.00000 0002)²)))÷(12·(X·0.00000 0001))'
«
	@@ Extra local variable(s).
	@@ ( -- d emptyProgram)
	1.0e-9
	« »

	→ f xv d generateOnePoint
	«
		@@ Generate one point.
		@@ ( w -- f((x * (1 + w * d))) )
		@@
		@@ In f(x) replace x with (x * (1 + w * d)). 
		«
			→ w
			«
				@@ ( -- f(x) )
				f
				@@ ( f(x) -- f(x) { x v } valuePosition )
				xv 2
				@@ ( ... -- x )
				xv 1 Get
				@@ ( x -- 'x * (1 + w * d)' )
				1 w d * + *
				@@ ( { x v } valuePostion 'x * (1 + w * d)' ) -- { x 'x * (1 + w * d)' } )
				Put
				@@ ( f(x) -- f((x * (1 + w * d))) )
				Where
			»
		»
		'generateOnePoint' Store

		@@ -f(x+2h) + 8 * f(x+h) -8 * f(x-h) + f(x-2h) =
		@@ (f(x+h) - f(x-h)) * 8 + (f(x-2h) - f(x+2h))
		+1 generateOnePoint
		-1 generateOnePoint
		-
		8 *
		-2 generateOnePoint
		+2 generateOnePoint
		-
		+
	
		@@ Divide by 12h. Recall that h = x * d.
		@@ Note that we are dividing by (a multiple of) x.
		@@ That could lead to dividing by 0, when x = 0.
		@@ But since we do not evaluate for p = x = v,
		@@ no harm will be done here.
		@@ It is up to the calling command to deal with x = 0.
		12
		@@ h = p * d
		xv 1 Get  d * *
		/
	»
»
